First, we use the distributive property to expand the first two factors:

\begin{align*}
4(x-5)(x+8) &= (4\cdot x - 4 \cdot 5) (x+8)\\
&=(4x-20)(x+8)
\end{align*}We use the distributive property again by adding the product of $4x-20$ and $x$ to the product of $4x-20$ and 8:

\begin{align*}
(4x-20)(x+8) &= (4x-20) \cdot x +(4x-20) \cdot 8\\
&= x(4x-20) + 8(4x-20)
\end{align*}
We use the distributive property again and combine like terms:

\begin{align*}
x(4x-20) + 8(4x-20) &= 4x^2 - 20x + 32x - 160\\
&= \boxed{4x^2 + 12x - 160}
\end{align*}

To solve for $x$, we wish to eliminate $y$. Multiply the first equation by $2$ and add it to the second: \begin{align*}
(4x-2y) + (x+2y) &= 10+5\\
5x &= 15\\
x &= \boxed{3}
\end{align*}

Let $a = e^{i \alpha},$ $b = e^{i \beta},$ and $c = e^{i \gamma}.$  Then
\begin{align*}
a + b + c &= e^{i \alpha} + e^{i \beta} + e^{i \gamma} \\
&= \cos \alpha + i \sin \alpha + \cos \beta + i \sin \beta + \cos \gamma + i \sin \gamma \\
&= (\cos \alpha + \cos \beta + \cos \gamma) + i (\sin \alpha + \sin \beta + \sin \gamma) \\
&= 1 + i.
\end{align*}Note that $|a| = |b| = |c| = 1.$  Then by the Triangle Inequality,
\[|a - (1 + i)| = |-b - c| \le |b| + |c| = 2.\]Thus, $a$ must lie in the disc centered at $1 + i$ with radius 2.  Also, $a$ must lie on the circle centered at 0 with radius 1.

